WEBVTT

00:01.001 --> 00:04.879
<i>♪ It seems today that all you see ♪</i>

00:04.880 --> 00:08.174
<i>♪ Is violence in movies and sex on TV ♪</i>

00:08.175 --> 00:11.928
<i>♪ But where are those
good old-fashioned values ♪</i>

00:11.929 --> 00:14.847
<i>♪ On which we used to rely? ♪</i>

00:14.848 --> 00:18.184
<i>♪ Lucky there's a family guy ♪</i>

00:18.185 --> 00:21.604
<i>♪ Lucky there's a man
who positively can do ♪</i>

00:21.605 --> 00:23.189
<i>♪ All the things that make us ♪</i>

00:23.190 --> 00:24.690
<i>♪ Laugh and cry ♪</i>

00:24.691 --> 00:30.155
<i>♪ He's... a... Fam... ily... Guy! ♪</i>

01:09.194 --> 01:12.030
Fart joke.

01:15.117 --> 01:16.659
Sir, you need to get ready

01:16.660 --> 01:19.578
for your lifetime achievement
award ceremony.

01:19.579 --> 01:21.414
Thank you, shape-shifting valet.

01:21.415 --> 01:24.292
Remember, sir, I can be
any shape you wish.

01:24.293 --> 01:26.795
Yeah, but you're already this, so...

01:33.844 --> 01:35.428
Excuse me.

01:35.429 --> 01:36.762
Pardon me.

01:36.763 --> 01:38.139
Beg your pardon.

01:38.140 --> 01:39.307
Coming through.

01:39.308 --> 01:40.433
Nice to see you.

01:40.434 --> 01:42.351
Thank you for coming.

01:46.648 --> 01:49.275
What if I told you you could accumulate

01:49.276 --> 01:51.193
all the wealth you'd ever want

01:51.194 --> 01:53.154
simply by learning
the secrets of real estate?

01:53.155 --> 01:54.447
Oop, wrong room.

01:54.448 --> 01:56.574
And then what if
you could use that wealth

01:56.575 --> 01:59.828
to turn yourself into a Broadway star?

02:11.381 --> 02:13.424
Welcome, ladies and gentlemen

02:13.425 --> 02:16.469
and 14 other genders we have now.

02:16.470 --> 02:17.887
I'm Lane Bergan,

02:17.888 --> 02:21.474
the biggest star of May 2020 and on.

02:21.475 --> 02:25.144
So, if you've only watched TV
up until April of 2020,

02:25.145 --> 02:27.938
my name would be unfamiliar to you.

02:27.939 --> 02:29.273
Lane Bergan?

02:29.274 --> 02:31.902
What, did Brett Kingston say no?

02:34.654 --> 02:38.407
When the Dwayne Johnson Center
for Confusing Ethnicity

02:38.408 --> 02:40.785
approached me about hosting this night,

02:40.786 --> 02:43.871
I said it'd be an honor to bestow upon

02:43.872 --> 02:48.501
Stewart Gilligan Griffin
our Lifetime Achievement Award.

02:48.502 --> 02:51.128
When Stewie invented the Wipeless Dump,

02:51.129 --> 02:54.840
our rainforests were
hanging on by a thread.

02:54.841 --> 02:57.968
Now, are there too many trees?

02:57.969 --> 03:01.013
Ladies and gentlemen, Stewart Griffin.

03:08.563 --> 03:10.356
Thank you for this wonderful honor.

03:12.692 --> 03:15.152
It's so wonderful to be
here with all of you.

03:16.363 --> 03:18.739
You guys mind stopping
for just one minute?

03:18.740 --> 03:22.201
When I heard I was going
to be receiving this award, I...

03:23.328 --> 03:24.703
I'm not the person who yells at waiters,

03:24.704 --> 03:27.581
but maybe everyone
bussing tables can freeze?

03:27.582 --> 03:29.542
I-I don't understand why I'm the person

03:29.543 --> 03:32.044
who has to be saying this, okay?

03:32.045 --> 03:34.505
Okay, I'll never forget
the first time I...

03:34.506 --> 03:37.466
Wow, really?

03:37.467 --> 03:39.427
This award means the world to...

03:40.554 --> 03:42.513
me...

03:42.514 --> 03:43.722
and I want to thank...

03:43.723 --> 03:46.392
everyone who...

03:46.393 --> 03:47.601
Anybody with a (BLEEP) bowtie on,

03:47.602 --> 03:49.687
stop what you're doing,
walk into the coatroom,

03:49.688 --> 03:52.440
and don't come out
until I'm done talking!

03:54.401 --> 03:57.236
I-I don't yell at waiters.

03:57.237 --> 03:58.779
I'm now going to stop mid-sentence

03:58.780 --> 04:01.491
because I see someone from my...

04:02.367 --> 04:03.993
Brian?

04:14.171 --> 04:16.380
So, Brian, how's Frank Sinatra, Jr.?

04:16.381 --> 04:19.300
- You two still hanging out?
- No. He died.

04:19.301 --> 04:22.970
I'll never forget it,
it was Spiro Agnew's birthday.

04:22.971 --> 04:24.972
Wow, so you, uh, really went all-in

04:24.973 --> 04:26.098
with the Japanese screens.

04:26.099 --> 04:28.476
Yes, I really like
changing in silhouette

04:28.477 --> 04:29.894
while carrying on a conversation.

04:29.895 --> 04:31.438
Will you excuse me?

04:33.899 --> 04:35.483
So, how was your flight?

04:35.484 --> 04:36.984
It was, uh, it was fine.

04:36.985 --> 04:38.986
I had a layover in Atlanta...

04:38.987 --> 04:40.446
What are you doing back there?

04:40.447 --> 04:42.781
Just getting into something
more comfortable.

04:42.782 --> 04:44.116
Can I interest you in a nightcap?

04:44.117 --> 04:45.534
- I think I've got...
- Who is that?

04:45.535 --> 04:47.786
A little privacy, please!

04:47.787 --> 04:49.288
What the hell was all that?

04:49.289 --> 04:51.123
I have a lot of money, Brian.

04:51.124 --> 04:54.794
But let's continue this while
I take a very foggy shower.

04:56.922 --> 04:58.130
No, Stewie, come on.

04:58.131 --> 05:00.132
I haven't seen you in almost 50 years.

05:00.133 --> 05:02.301
And you haven't even
told me how great I look.

05:02.302 --> 05:04.595
You do look great. Thanks to me.

05:04.596 --> 05:06.847
I invented a pill to extend your life.

05:06.848 --> 05:08.933
It's called "Semper Fido."

05:08.934 --> 05:10.434
What? Why?

05:10.435 --> 05:12.853
Aren't you going to say anything
about the cute name I gave it?

05:12.854 --> 05:14.855
Ha. What? Why?

05:14.856 --> 05:16.315
I snuck it in your food
because I wanted you

05:16.316 --> 05:19.568
to live long enough to see that
global warming is bull crap.

05:19.569 --> 05:21.779
Oh, my God, we were so wrong about that.

05:21.780 --> 05:23.531
If anything, it's way colder now.

05:23.532 --> 05:24.865
Yes, and now thanks to you,

05:24.866 --> 05:27.034
we're stuck with President Polar Bear.

05:27.035 --> 05:29.912
President Polar Bear, is it true
you ate the presidential seal?

05:29.913 --> 05:31.956
That was a simple misunderstanding.

05:31.957 --> 05:33.916
- No further questions.
- President Polar Bear!

05:33.917 --> 05:36.126
President Polar Bear,
what did you do for a Klondike bar?

05:36.127 --> 05:40.089
I believe the president has
answered all of your questions.

05:40.090 --> 05:41.590
Here's what I don't understand...

05:41.591 --> 05:43.467
Why did you even want me
to live this long

05:43.468 --> 05:44.677
if you were just gonna leave me?

05:44.678 --> 05:46.178
It's not about you, Brian.

05:46.179 --> 05:49.431
- I couldn't take it back there.
- But they were your family, Stewie.

05:49.432 --> 05:51.684
I guess I'm just not a family guy.

05:53.061 --> 05:56.356
Mom and Dad always wanted me
to be someone I wasn't.

05:58.858 --> 06:01.777
Stewie Griffin, get in here right now!

06:01.778 --> 06:03.153
- Yeah?
- Well,

06:03.154 --> 06:05.489
I just got our Christmas card photos.

06:05.490 --> 06:07.992
You want to tell me what you're
doing with your hands here?

06:07.993 --> 06:09.994
- Nothing.
- Exactly, nothing.

06:09.995 --> 06:12.538
And what does the greeting
at the top of the card say?

06:12.539 --> 06:14.873
"Merry Christmas
and a Shocking New Year."

06:14.874 --> 06:16.709
And what is every
other member of the family

06:16.710 --> 06:17.960
doing with their hands?

06:17.961 --> 06:19.670
- The shocker.
- Right.

06:19.671 --> 06:21.839
Now, listen, Stewie,
I'm a cool dad, all right?

06:21.840 --> 06:24.842
I could care less what you
do with the pink, truly.

06:24.843 --> 06:27.511
But the stink is where
you get the "shocking."

06:27.512 --> 06:29.221
You get that? You get what I'm saying?

06:29.222 --> 06:31.140
Even if it's just one, that's fine.

06:31.141 --> 06:33.892
- But you got to put something there.
- I-I think it's gonna be fine.

06:33.893 --> 06:35.519
I'm sure people won't even notice.

06:37.063 --> 06:38.480
Oh...

06:38.481 --> 06:40.024
Anyway, that's why I left.

06:40.025 --> 06:41.734
Well, that was a long time ago.

06:41.735 --> 06:42.985
You have to come back.

06:42.986 --> 06:44.528
Stewie...

06:44.529 --> 06:46.488
- Peter is dying.
- What?

06:46.489 --> 06:48.574
Oh, my God, that's awful.

06:48.575 --> 06:50.909
- So, you'll come see him?
- Of course.

06:50.910 --> 06:52.119
You know, he once asked me in the event

06:52.120 --> 06:55.080
that he was sick
to clear his Google history.

06:55.081 --> 06:58.168
"Peter Griffin search history."

06:58.627 --> 06:59.918
"Winnie the Pooh,

06:59.919 --> 07:01.754
"Winnie the Pooh jacket,

07:01.755 --> 07:03.881
"Winnie the Pooh vintage jacket,

07:03.882 --> 07:05.799
"Winnie the Pooh letterman jacket,

07:05.800 --> 07:07.885
"Winnie the Pooh windbreaker,

07:07.886 --> 07:09.470
"Eeyore jacket,

07:09.471 --> 07:11.513
"Eeyore vintage jacket,

07:11.514 --> 07:13.474
"Eeyore letterman jacket,

07:13.475 --> 07:15.476
lactating pregnant Latinas..."

07:15.477 --> 07:17.311
Wow. Huge turn there.

07:17.312 --> 07:18.812
"Piglet pencil erasers."

07:18.813 --> 07:20.230
Okay, getting back in there.

07:20.231 --> 07:22.900
"Full cast Winnie the Pooh backpack."

07:22.901 --> 07:25.444
Oh, "cancer symptoms," yeah.

07:25.445 --> 07:27.946
"Coughing up blood, pain in abdomen,

07:27.947 --> 07:28.947
Winnie the Pooh casket."

07:28.948 --> 07:31.116
Yeah, he is sick.
You know, while we're here,

07:31.117 --> 07:32.826
<i>let's take a look
at your search history.</i>

07:32.827 --> 07:35.954
- No, Stewie, that's...
- "Spiro Agnew birthday."

07:35.955 --> 07:39.376
What a weird thing to try
to impress me with.

07:44.839 --> 07:46.924
Okay, first stop, Chris Griffin.

07:46.925 --> 07:49.718
- We have to pick up Chris?
- Yeah, what's the problem?

07:49.719 --> 07:51.845
Uh, we didn't exactly
get along too well.

07:51.846 --> 07:55.683
<i>Especially after Grandpa died
and left me the dark boathouse.</i>

07:55.684 --> 07:57.059
You can still use the boathouse

07:57.060 --> 07:59.770
on non-vacation Sundays in the spring.

07:59.771 --> 08:01.647
I've always taken care of you, Chris.

08:01.648 --> 08:03.273
Taken care of me?

08:03.274 --> 08:06.485
<i>You're my kid brother,
you take care of me?</i>

08:06.486 --> 08:08.112
Sorry, I came down here to vape.

08:08.113 --> 08:11.615
Send Chris off to do this,
send Chris off to do that.

08:11.616 --> 08:13.409
I'm supposed to be
shoveling the driveway.

08:13.410 --> 08:17.496
I'm your older brother, Stewie,
and I was stepped over!

08:17.497 --> 08:19.248
It's the way Grandpa wanted it.

08:19.249 --> 08:21.291
It ain't the way I wanted it!

08:21.292 --> 08:23.001
Sounds like you're having
a personal conversation.

08:23.002 --> 08:25.921
- I'll put in my earbuds.
- I'm smart!

08:25.922 --> 08:28.549
Not like everybody says, like dumb.

08:28.550 --> 08:31.176
I'm smart and I want respect.

08:31.177 --> 08:33.513
♪ Funky Cold Medina. ♪

08:39.394 --> 08:41.437
Chris, you live in filth.

08:41.438 --> 08:44.481
- What have you been doing?
- Yeah, I kind of wasted my life,

08:44.482 --> 08:47.568
except I obsessed over
teaching my penis how to talk.

08:47.569 --> 08:49.361
- What?
- Who's out there?

08:49.362 --> 08:51.280
Settle down, just got some company.

08:51.281 --> 08:53.449
Well, aren't you going to introduce me?

08:53.450 --> 08:56.076
I'm getting to it,
if-if you'll give me a second.

08:56.077 --> 08:57.745
I want to have a look at them.

08:57.746 --> 09:00.706
Hey, numbskull, that's how we
got in trouble the last time.

09:01.708 --> 09:04.001
He-he's really very friendly.

09:04.002 --> 09:05.836
Where's the Jamba
Juice you were gonna get me?

09:05.837 --> 09:08.297
Never mind, I'll order it on Postmates.

09:08.298 --> 09:11.676
No, you won't.
Stop spending all our money.

09:15.346 --> 09:17.097
So, what's Meg been up to anyway?

09:17.098 --> 09:19.725
She runs a small
private security business

09:19.726 --> 09:20.726
