09:20.727 --> 09:21.977
That sounds kind of cool.

09:21.978 --> 09:25.481
Well, she basically just
tests bulletproof vests.

09:26.775 --> 09:28.358
- Ready?
- One sec.

09:30.028 --> 09:31.737
Yeah, go, go, go.

09:35.575 --> 09:37.701
Ooh... yeah.

09:42.957 --> 09:45.042
This one can use another layer.

09:45.043 --> 09:46.794
Oh, hey, guys.

09:46.795 --> 09:49.463
- Um, are you okay?
- Yeah, I'll be fine.

09:49.464 --> 09:51.590
Hi, Meg. Bring it in.

09:51.591 --> 09:52.800
Hi, Chris' Penis.

09:52.801 --> 09:53.926
How are you?

09:53.927 --> 09:56.387
Same spit, different day.

10:00.975 --> 10:02.935
Wow, look at Quahog.

10:02.936 --> 10:05.771
Light rail system, gleaming skyscrapers.

10:05.772 --> 10:07.064
♪ Weenie and the Butt. ♪

10:07.065 --> 10:09.441
But somehow, the same morning DJs.

10:09.442 --> 10:11.693
<i>♪ Quahog 97 ♪</i>

10:11.694 --> 10:14.029
<i>♪ FM on the radio ♪</i>

10:14.030 --> 10:15.656
<i>♪ And the Internet ♪</i>

10:15.657 --> 10:17.241
<i>♪ And the orb ♪</i>

10:17.242 --> 10:19.034
<i>♪ A new invention ♪</i>

10:19.035 --> 10:20.661
<i>♪ Which lets you hear stuff ♪</i>

10:20.662 --> 10:22.204
<i>♪ Right in your head ♪</i>

10:22.205 --> 10:23.705
<i>♪ Without a device. ♪</i>

10:23.706 --> 10:25.249
<i>Try turning it off.</i>

10:25.250 --> 10:27.876
<i>- You can't!
- That's not all that hasn't changed.</i>

10:27.877 --> 10:30.420
Cleveland's still on hold
with United Airlines.

10:35.009 --> 10:38.762
I'm starting to think my call
is not important to them.

10:38.763 --> 10:40.556
<i>Your call is important to us.</i>

10:40.557 --> 10:42.516
<i>Thank you for remaining on the line.</i>

10:42.517 --> 10:46.144
All right, you just bought
yourself another year.

10:46.145 --> 10:48.730
And Seamus is still on hold
with Spirit Airlines.

10:48.731 --> 10:51.108
<i>We don't give a crap
about you, but we're the cheapest,</i>

10:51.109 --> 10:54.653
<i>- so sit there and take it.
- Ah, sea turds.</i>

10:55.697 --> 10:58.991
Mr. Seamus, five minutes
to showtime, Mr. Seamus.

10:58.992 --> 11:01.118
Oh, I want to fly standby to Pittsburgh,

11:01.119 --> 11:04.246
<i>but I also want to host The Muppet Show.</i>

11:09.335 --> 11:11.086
Look at all this traffic.

11:11.087 --> 11:13.797
Yeah, Brady Boulevard
is tight this time of day.

11:13.798 --> 11:16.133
You know what?
Cut over to Brady on Brady

11:16.134 --> 11:18.010
and then take the Brady Bridge.

11:18.011 --> 11:20.721
Is everything in this town
named after Tom Brady?

11:20.722 --> 11:23.390
Oh, no, there's the
Rob Gronkowski Library.

11:23.391 --> 11:26.518
The only book is just a label
ripped off a Muscle Milk bottle.

11:26.519 --> 11:29.146
And look, there's the
Robert Kraft Marina,

11:29.147 --> 11:31.315
full of tugboats.

11:31.316 --> 11:33.902
I heard he had a stroke.

11:36.237 --> 11:37.863
I can't even get my bearings.

11:37.864 --> 11:39.197
I'm gonna ask someone for directions.

11:39.198 --> 11:40.908
I wouldn't do that. Since you left,

11:40.909 --> 11:43.744
the New England accent
has become incomprehensible.

11:43.745 --> 11:45.037
I'm sure it's not that bad.

11:45.038 --> 11:48.040
Excuse me, sir,
where is the Quahog Harbor?

11:48.041 --> 11:49.833
- Cah gabbah?
- What?

11:49.834 --> 11:51.752
I-I just, I just want to know
where the Quahog Harbor is.

11:51.753 --> 11:52.878
Cah gabbah.

11:52.879 --> 11:54.838
Uh-oh, there's a lot of guys

11:54.839 --> 11:57.007
in Bruins hats turning around now.

11:57.008 --> 11:59.384
- Abbah dabbah.
- Gwin' dahsee da Sawx.

11:59.385 --> 12:00.409
N'abbah dabbah.

12:00.410 --> 12:01.970
- Cah gabbah.
- Gwin' dahsee da Sawx.

12:06.643 --> 12:08.770
Aah! Brian, get out of here. Go, go, go!

12:12.065 --> 12:14.066
Christopher "Irish or Italian name,"

12:14.067 --> 12:16.276
are you causing trouble out there?

12:16.277 --> 12:17.903
- No, Ma.
- Nomah?

12:17.904 --> 12:20.531
- Nomah!
- Nomah!

12:27.705 --> 12:29.581
What the hell happened
to the neighborhood?

12:29.582 --> 12:32.709
Hey, Stewie.
Here comes a double scoop of trouble.

12:32.710 --> 12:35.212
Whoa, you look great,
considering your age.

12:35.213 --> 12:36.797
Yeah, I'm basically exactly the same,

12:36.798 --> 12:39.299
except I pretty much only talk
about ice cream now.

12:39.300 --> 12:42.636
- Oh, that's cool, that's cool.
- Yeah, you know what's cool? Ice cream.

12:42.637 --> 12:46.473
- Want to go get a cup? Cone? Bowl?
- I-I'm just trying to see my folks.

12:46.474 --> 12:47.683
Man, I love ice cream.

12:47.684 --> 12:50.102
You know there's three different
ice cream shops in Quahog?

12:50.103 --> 12:51.937
- They're all good.
- What's your favorite?

12:51.938 --> 12:53.398
They're all good.

12:54.065 --> 12:55.983
So that's the scoop from here.

12:55.984 --> 12:58.903
All right, well,
good running into you, man.

13:00.279 --> 13:02.990
Oh, my babies,
finally all together again.

13:02.991 --> 13:06.284
Hello, Mother.
I mean, uh, damn you, vile woman.

13:06.285 --> 13:08.453
I must kill you, et cetera, et cetera.

13:10.581 --> 13:12.499
Did Quagmire tell you
about the ice cream?

13:12.500 --> 13:13.542
Yes.

13:13.543 --> 13:16.378
You know, there are three
ice cream parlors in town.

13:16.379 --> 13:18.005
- We know.
- They're all good.

13:18.006 --> 13:20.173
- Yes, he said that.
- They're all good.

13:20.174 --> 13:22.843
Have we already run out of conversation?

13:22.844 --> 13:24.636
Chris, Meg, how are you?

13:24.637 --> 13:26.471
- Good, Ma.
- How are you?

13:26.472 --> 13:28.974
Oh, I can't complain.
Little hard of hearing,

13:28.975 --> 13:31.226
which is why I turned on
the closed captioning.

13:31.227 --> 13:33.187
It's about 30 seconds behind, though.

13:34.689 --> 13:36.648
Wow, that is way behind.

13:36.649 --> 13:38.483
Now, what would you kids
like for dinner?

13:38.484 --> 13:41.904
- It's 3:15, Ma.
- I know, we waited for you.

13:46.159 --> 13:48.493
Yeah, we-we can go ahead
and turn that off.

13:48.494 --> 13:49.871
How's Dad?

13:53.708 --> 13:56.001
Your father's had severe diabetes

13:56.002 --> 13:59.004
ever since they opened
three ice cream stores in town.

13:59.005 --> 14:00.922
They're all good.

14:00.923 --> 14:03.383
You can't live like this,
the house is falling apart.

14:03.384 --> 14:05.552
This is awful, and it's all my fault.

14:05.553 --> 14:08.346
Oh, Pop, I am so sorry
I abandoned you all.

14:08.347 --> 14:11.016
I never should've left home.
What can I do?

14:11.017 --> 14:15.353
Just promise, when I die,
that you will help our family.

14:15.354 --> 14:17.439
I will, I promise.

14:17.440 --> 14:20.984
This family will never want
for anything ever again.

14:20.985 --> 14:22.778
- That's so generous.
- Thank you.

14:22.779 --> 14:24.237
Chris, your hand.

14:24.238 --> 14:25.906
All right, now that that's settled,

14:25.907 --> 14:27.824
let's celebrate
with some of the music of now

14:27.825 --> 14:29.786
with closed captioning.

14:30.828 --> 14:33.955
<i>♪ Music of now, music of now ♪</i>

14:33.956 --> 14:38.169
<i>♪ Music of now, music of now,
music of now. ♪</i>

14:46.511 --> 14:49.221
Good afternoon, I'm Tom Tucker,
delivering the news

14:49.222 --> 14:52.140
with my Andy Rooney
end-of-life eyebrows.

14:52.141 --> 14:53.767
You won't hear anything I'm saying

14:53.768 --> 14:55.268
because they're so distracting.

14:55.269 --> 14:57.979
Now, let's go to Asian reporter
Tricia Takanawa,

14:57.980 --> 15:01.274
so we can be shocked at how well
her people age. Tricia?

15:01.275 --> 15:04.236
Tom, I'm standing here
with flawless skin

15:04.237 --> 15:08.073
next to the shedding, crumbling,
dusty ancient relics

15:08.074 --> 15:11.076
of white people my age.

15:12.912 --> 15:15.997
Oh, Stewie, you've done so much
to help our family.

15:15.998 --> 15:18.333
I can't believe you put in an elevator.

15:18.334 --> 15:21.128
Yes, and it even has elevator music.

15:21.129 --> 15:25.006
<i>♪ Music of now, music of now. ♪</i>

15:25.007 --> 15:27.843
Aw, and thanks for these
virtual reality glasses,

15:27.844 --> 15:30.762
so I can watch porn
while talking to the family.

15:30.763 --> 15:33.849
So what's California like, Stewie? Ugh.

15:33.850 --> 15:35.183
That was a penis.

15:35.184 --> 15:38.311
So, do-do you still want to know
about California?

15:38.312 --> 15:39.355
No, I'm done.

15:40.940 --> 15:42.774
I have one more dying wish.

15:42.775 --> 15:46.612
Play the song, but play it slow
because I am old.

15:47.488 --> 15:51.158
<i>♪ A-well-a everybody's heard ♪</i>

15:51.159 --> 15:53.869
<i>♪ About the bird... ♪</i>

15:53.870 --> 15:56.329
Family, help me dance.

15:56.330 --> 15:58.039
<i>♪ B-bird's a word ♪</i>

15:58.040 --> 16:00.208
<i>♪ A-well, a bird, bird, bird... ♪</i>

16:00.209 --> 16:02.502
- How long, Peter?
- I'll say when.

16:02.503 --> 16:05.213
<i>♪ A-well, a bird, bird, bird ♪</i>

16:05.214 --> 16:08.049
<i>♪ Well-a bird is a word ♪</i>

16:08.050 --> 16:12.262
<i>♪ A-well, a bird, bird, bird,
b-bird's a word ♪</i>

16:12.263 --> 16:15.473
<i>♪ A-well, a bird, bird, bird ♪</i>

16:15.474 --> 16:17.268
<i>♪ Well-a bird is a word. ♪</i>

16:23.941 --> 16:26.193
Oh, Dr. Hartman, thank you for coming.

16:26.194 --> 16:28.361
Actually, I'm Dr. Hartman's son.

16:28.362 --> 16:31.448
Doctor Hartmanson?
But I asked for Dr. Hartman.

16:31.449 --> 16:33.200
His jokes are getting worse, Doctor.

16:33.201 --> 16:35.411
Is there anything you can do for him?

16:36.245 --> 16:38.623
Now all we can do is wait.

16:41.209 --> 16:44.002
Lois... it's time.

16:44.003 --> 16:47.715
Oh, Peter, I'm gonna miss you so much.

16:50.051 --> 16:51.968
I see a white light.

16:51.969 --> 16:54.095
There are others inside of it.

16:54.096 --> 16:56.640
Adam West, Carrie Fisher,

16:56.641 --> 16:59.142
Ricardo Montalb├бn, Phyllis Diller...

16:59.143 --> 17:01.853
Heaven is filled
with every actor who ever died?

17:01.854 --> 17:04.356
No, this is actually
just the ones who did our show

17:04.357 --> 17:06.274
right before they died. Crazy, right?

17:06.275 --> 17:09.277
Frank Sinatra Jr., Charles Durning,

17:09.278 --> 17:11.863
Lauren Bacall, Rodney Dangerfield,

17:11.864 --> 17:14.115
Roy Scheider, Waylon Jennings,

17:14.116 --> 17:16.618
Ed Asner by the time
this airs certainly...

17:16.619 --> 17:19.287
Dad, you don't have to do this,
there are too many.

17:19.288 --> 17:22.249
Uh-oh, Conway Twitty is here,
and he's pissed.

17:22.250 --> 17:24.125
Wait, he's wearing
the Darth Vader helmet.

17:24.126 --> 17:27.003
Never mind, he was cool with it.

17:27.004 --> 17:30.257
This is it.

17:32.468 --> 17:35.011
Oh, he's trying to say something.

17:35.012 --> 17:37.097
H-His final words.

17:37.098 --> 17:38.306
Lactating...

17:38.307 --> 17:41.142
pregnant... Latinas.

17:41.143 --> 17:44.814
I will, Dad, I promise.

17:56.325 --> 18:00.496
No, we won't cry for him,
we will celebrate his life.

18:00.497 --> 18:03.999
The finest cigars for
the finest family ever to live.

18:04.000 --> 18:06.793
Oh, Stewie, we love you so much.

18:06.794 --> 18:10.797
And I love you, which is why
I must not delay any longer.

18:10.798 --> 18:14.718
I must get my affairs in order
and transfer my money to all of you.

18:14.719 --> 18:17.345
- I will see you all soon.
- Oh, thank you, Stewie.

18:17.346 --> 18:19.181
- We love you.
- Thanks.

18:42.038 --> 18:43.747
We did it. We got him.

18:43.748 --> 18:45.749
<i>I feel like we're in The Sting,</i>

18:45.750 --> 18:49.252
that movie from 100 years ago
about 150 years ago.

18:49.253 --> 18:51.296
Great work tricking him, Brian.

18:51.297 --> 18:54.132
Thanks. Well, you know,
I credit my years as a writer.

18:54.133 --> 18:56.217
When I planned the con,
I saw Quahog as a character...

18:56.218 --> 18:57.678
Okay, that's enough.

19:07.688 --> 19:09.522
<i>Had a pebble in my shoe.</i>

19:09.523 --> 19:12.025
<i>Of course I knew
the whole thing was a scam.</i>

19:12.026 --> 19:14.778
<i>They probably did that "crying
turning into laughing" thing</i>

19:14.779 --> 19:16.821
<i>when I left, what a bunch of hacks.</i>

19:16.822 --> 19:19.282
<i>They're too stupid to notice
I snuck into the kitchen</i>

19:19.283 --> 19:21.659
<i>and turned up the gas before I left.</i>

19:21.660 --> 19:24.622
<i>Chris should be lighting
his cigar right about...</i>

19:26.832 --> 19:29.459
Stewie, help.

19:29.460 --> 19:32.712
It hurts! Reverse the pill! Let me die!

19:32.713 --> 19:37.175
Ooh, wish I could, but the pills
were in the house, so, yeah...

19:37.176 --> 19:39.260
Stewie. Stewie!

19:39.261 --> 19:42.514
Stewie! Stewie!

19:42.515 --> 19:44.557
Stewie! Stewie!

19:44.558 --> 19:46.518
Huh? What?

19:46.519 --> 19:48.186
What the hell is wrong with you?
You've been staring

19:48.187 --> 19:50.939
at that old man Halloween
costume for 30 minutes.

19:50.940 --> 19:54.317
21 plus commercials,
but it's a big decision.

19:54.318 --> 19:56.694
You know, I've always been
afraid of being old,

19:56.695 --> 19:59.490
but now I think I'll like it just fine.

20:05.246 --> 20:07.831
Why are you walking so slowly?

20:07.832 --> 20:10.708
Turns out this costume
is about 80% balls,

20:10.709 --> 20:14.087
and most of it's dragging behind me.

20:15.131 --> 20:18.258
- Uhp, we got a tangle.
- Uhp, what do I do?

20:18.259 --> 20:20.593
Stop walking.
I'll go back, you go forward.

20:20.594 --> 20:21.845
- Are you sure?
- It's counterintuitive.

20:21.846 --> 20:23.304
I don't know, that-that
doesn't seem right to me.

20:23.305 --> 20:24.431
When you want to go left, you go right.

20:24.432 --> 20:25.473
I'm just gonna pull forward.

20:25.474 --> 20:26.724
- Don't pull, don't pull.
- I-I think if you come this way,

20:26.725 --> 20:28.268
- and I go that way...
- Just stop walking and listen to me.

20:28.269 --> 20:29.811
Everybody freeze.

20:29.812 --> 20:32.231
Okay, let's just think about this.

20:38.028 --> 20:40.738
People of Argentina,

20:40.739 --> 20:42.615
I have heard your cries,

20:42.616 --> 20:44.033
and I just want to say...

20:44.034 --> 20:45.952
Meg. Meg!

20:45.953 --> 20:48.288
I already told you
you're not gonna be Evita.

20:48.289 --> 20:50.915
You're gonna be the back half
of Edgar the Farting Horse.

20:50.916 --> 20:52.168
Now get in.

20:56.839 --> 20:58.924
Hey. I do the farting.